# Docker Compose secrets — copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill
# in what you need. See the root README's "Secrets — running this
# independently of the author" section for the full explanation. Short
# version:
#
#   JWT_SECRET           — self-contained, safe to generate yourself. Only
#                           auth-service and api-gateway need to agree on
#                           the value; nothing external checks it.
#                             macOS/Linux : openssl rand -base64 32
#                             Windows     : powershell -Command
#                               "[Convert]::ToBase64String((1..32|%{Get-Random -Max 256}))"
#                           Leaving this unset still works — auth-service
#                           and api-gateway fall back to the loud, obviously
#                           insecure default already in
#                           config-repo/application.properties.
#
#   SMTP_PASSWORD         — a REAL external credential (a Gmail App
#                           Password), not something you can generate.
#                           Leave this unset unless it's your own account —
#                           notification-service gracefully falls back to
#                           recording notifications instead of emailing
#                           them (see NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL below), so the
#                           full order -> notification flow still works
#                           with nothing set here.
#
#   NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL  — "log" (default, no credentials needed — records
#                           every notification with channel "IN_APP") or
#                           "email" (real Gmail SMTP send — requires
#                           SMTP_PASSWORD to actually succeed, otherwise the
#                           notification is recorded as "FAILED").
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL — where the frontend should call the gateway.
#                           Defaults to the gateway's Compose host port
#                           mapping; only change this if you remapped
#                           api-gateway's host port in docker-compose.yml.

JWT_SECRET=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL=log
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9090/api
